## 📄 What you’ll need at pick‑up

1. **Valid driver’s licence** (must be in English or accompanied by an International Driving Permit).  
2. **Credit card** in the driver’s name (used for the deposit and any extra charges).  
3. **Passport / ID** (for verification).  
4. **Reservation confirmation** (the search key above can be used if you contact Europcar directly).  

---

## 📌 Important Terms & Conditions

| Condition | Details |
|-----------|---------|
| **One‑way fee** | A non‑refundable fee of **US $4 545.45** is applied because the car is being dropped off in a different city (Perth). |
| **Fuel policy** | Return the car with the same fuel level you received it (full‑to‑full). |
| **Mileage** | Unlimited – you can drive as many kilometres as you like without extra charge. |
| **Cancellation** | Free cancellation is available up to the supplier’s deadline (usually 24 h before pick‑up). Check the exact time in the confirmation email. |
| **Amendments** | You may change dates/times without a fee, but any price difference will be applied. |
| **Insurance** | The quoted price includes the basic “collision damage waiver” (CDW) and theft protection that the supplier offers under the “No‑OP‑AQ‑USES” and “SUPPRESS_FEE_FIXED_PRICE_VEHICLES” features. Additional coverage (e.g., personal accident insurance) can be purchased at the desk. |
| **Age restrictions** | Drivers must be at least **21 years old**; drivers under 25 may incur a young‑driver surcharge (already factored into the quoted price). |
| **Additional driver** | You can add extra drivers for a small daily fee (usually US $10‑$15 per driver). |

